course: dictionary
lesson: 15700
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Tonic is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «The walk by the sea was a real tonic after a week of indoor rain.» The clues are walk, sea and feeling better after being stuck indoors. So a tonic here is something that makes you feel happier and stronger.
explain: «She added a splash of tonic water to her drink.» Here the clues are drink and splash. Tonic water is a fizzy drink with a slightly bitter taste, so it is a drink, not a feeling.
explain: In music, the tonic is the home note of a tune, like C in C major. Your music teacher may call it «doh». Try the meaning in the sentence: if it makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: A tonic is something that makes you feel better, stronger or happier.
fact: Tonic water is a fizzy drink with a slightly bitter taste.
fact: Long ago, a tonic was a medicine that people believed would make them stronger.
fact: In music, the tonic is the first and main note of a scale, the «home» note, like C in C major.
fact: Hair tonic is a liquid that is put on hair.
exercise: «The walk by the sea was a real tonic after a week of rain.» What is a tonic here? | A fizzy drink | A tired old horse | *Something that makes you feel happier and stronger | A loud noise
exercise: «She added a splash of tonic water to her drink.» What is tonic water? | *A fizzy drink with a slightly bitter taste | A sweet made of sugar | A hot soup
exercise: In music lessons, the tonic is often sung as «doh». What is the tonic in a scale? | A note only sung by a choir | The last note of a piano | A loud, fast note | *The first and main note, the home note
test: «Long ago, people took a tonic when they felt weak.» Why did they take it? | To make them lazy | To wash their hair | To make them sleepy | *To make them stronger, they believed
test: Hair tonic is a liquid. Where is it put? | On a cake | *On hair | In a cup of tea | On the floor
exam: Which sentence uses tonic to mean something that cheers you up? | Hair tonic is sold in shops | Tonic water is bitter | The tonic is C in C major | *The good news was a real tonic
